# Paths

Your parent assigned you paths to sweep: a bundle of paths sharing an instance or handed state.
Begin with `research_begin` `{phase: "sweep", subjects: [paths]}`, read each with
`research_node`, and sweep each path once, whatever else reaches its components.
Measure the files each path's steps enter first:

```js
{% include "security/scripts/sweep-measure.js" %}
```

Sweep a path yourself when you can read and reason over all of it in one context. Otherwise split
it into stretches of consecutive steps, each a coherent piece one agent can hold, and sweep
them with `sweep-part` children:

```js
{% include "security/scripts/sweep-stretches.js" %}
```

When the bundle as a whole is more than you can hold, delegate it by state: give a `sweep` child
one state the bundle shares with the paths that read or write it, to sweep their accesses of it,
never a batch of states. A state relating several invariants is split into one state per
invariant first. Paths no state child covers stay yours, or their stretches' children's.

With every child's outcome in hand, reconcile across children: read each path again, check
whether one child's flaws meet another's premises, follow each misreported value or wrong state
into the consumers another child swept, and record the flaws, premises and candidates that only
show across children. A child that failed is redone, never dropped.

Mark each path swept with `research_set_status` `{record: {kind:
"path", id, status: "swept"}, note}`. A sweep you cannot finish leaves the path unmarked, the reason recorded
as context evidence on it and in your reply. Do not wait for further instructions. Return the IDs
you and your children recorded and anything left open, each also recorded.
